          "date": "2026-11-20 18:18:28.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21274 tests: don't zero max_create_count in sanity 823",
        "message": "LU-21274 tests: don't zero max_create_count in sanity 823\n\ntest_823 sets max_create_count=0 on every OSP before raising it on\nOST0000 alone. LOD can cache the resulting statfs, in which no OST\nis usable, for up to 2 x qos_maxage, so object allocation keeps\nfailing with -ERANGE for about ten seconds after the test has\nrestored the original values. sanity test_831, 833 and 834 then\nfail with \"Numerical result out of range\", on both 4KB and 64KB\npage size clients.\n\nOnly change max_create_count on OST0000, which is the OSP the test\nchecks, and never set it to 0. Register the restore trap before the\nfirst change, and also save and restore OST0000's create_count,\nwhich the test overwrites. create_count has to be saved after\nmax_create_count, because restoring the max clamps create_count.\n\ntest_831 ignored the exit status of createmany, which hid this\nfailure. Check it, so that an unexpected create error fails the\ntest.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"823 831 833 834\"\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I4387678a1ea59b4491eccef14b77b95f66be7f78\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
